From: Vedant Bhale <vedant.bhale@ymail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Link SDL into the shared LVGL library
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [appliance-specific SDL configuration]
Signed-off-by: Vedant Bhale <vedant.bhale@ymail.com>

SDL is enabled in this LVGL build, so liblvgl.so must declare SDL as a
runtime dependency. Linking only the video executable leaves the launcher
with unresolved SDL symbols at boot.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@
   include(${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/env_support/cmake/custom.cmake)
 endif()
 
+# LVGL's SDL display driver is included in this appliance's shared library.
+target_link_libraries(lvgl PRIVATE SDL2)
+
 #[[
     unfortunately CMAKE_WINDOWS_EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS does not work for global data. 
     for global data we still need decl specs.
